// fixture for comlint_globalshadow.comt -- comlint's INPUT, never run
// directly (never registered in run_all.comt). Every bare write below
// lands in a real global with nothing shadowing/clearing it, so
// comlint should flag every name -- gs_dotfunc's write sits inside
// obj.func(...), a method call on obj literally named "func", not the
// func(...) closure-literal builtin, so it does not get that builtin's
// own-frame suppression; gs_reclear is re-declared with a fresh
// global(gs_reclear)=2 after being cleared, which un-clears it.

global(gs_p)=1
gs_p=2

global(gs_dotfunc)=1
obj.func(gs_dotfunc=2)

global(gs_reclear)=1
global(gs_reclear :clear)
global(gs_reclear)=2
gs_reclear=3
